  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan names it among the ten earths, the unique terrains the world called by that name after the five regions became one, the two heavens combined, and the earth veins of the five regions merged; both statements of the set print the name Treasure Earth. The other nine are Earth Abyss, Earth Trench, Earth Tunnel, Earth Cave, Earth Prison, Production Earth, Flying Earth, Formation Earth, and Tomb Earth.",
      "chapters": [
        2058
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "reg_earth_earth_abyss",
        "reg_earth_earth_trench",
        "reg_earth_earth_tunnel",
        "reg_earth_earth_cave",
        "gu_earth_prison",
        "reg_earth_production_earth",
        "reg_earth_flying_earth",
        "reg_earth_formation_earth",
        "reg_earth_tomb_earth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Bai Ning Bing wakes in a cave whose form is like a sphere, with the group at the bottom. The inner walls have large patches of scattered yellow soil. From time to time, red lights flash as if flowing on the yellow soil and condensing into blood veins. Immortal materials sit embedded in the walls at set intervals, including domination copper, white snow iron, white wine turnip, profound eerie wind, and many others across paths. Crystal essences of many paths appear, but earth blood veins buried in the soil are highest in quantity. At intervals they shine and flow like blood capillaries. Their source is a delicate little black-yellow heart from which net-like blood veins spread. That heart is a luck path immortal material.",
      "chapters": [
        2076
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_bai_ning_bing",
        "sys_immortal_material"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The three immortals first guess Hu Land, then reject it.",
      "chapters": [
        2076
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_hu_land"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan later names the place Earth Treasury, one of the ten earths. Every Earth Treasury holds abundant immortal materials, especially the rank nine luck path immortal material favored heart. He finds them still alive and trapped in an earth vein, hiding in Earth Treasury.",
      "chapters": [
        2078
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the heart of the mighty earth vein he withstands the pressure and stores the whole Earth Treasury into his immortal aperture.",
      "chapters": [
        2079
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Southern Border’s Paradise Earth true inheritance describes the ten earths in detail and states that they can bear the task of being earth vein nodes. It is not among the five Fang Yuan can create while he builds an artificial earth vein; those are Earth Abyss, Earth Trench, Earth Tunnel, Production Earth, and Formation Earth, and the other five are beyond his ability at that point.",
      "chapters": [
        2142
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "earth-vein-node",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_southern_border",
        "inh_paradise_earth_true_inheritance"
      ]
    }
  ],
